  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Energy obligated $6.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The Department of Energy awarded 577 contracts with an average award size of $10.8M. The Department of Energy's obligations are down 88.7% year over year. The Department of Energy's FY2027 total is partial because current-year totals are fiscal year to date. The Department of Energy's obligations in the five prior full fiscal years were: FY22 $41.2B, FY23 $44.6B, FY24 $46B, FY25 $48.5B, and FY26 $55.1B. The Department of Energy concentrated FY2027 to date spending in Facilities Support Services at $3.5B and in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $1.1B. The Department of Energy's top vendors in FY2027 to date include TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $875M and NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC at $633M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is Energy's FY2027 contract program so far?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy obligated $6.2B in FY2027 to date. The Department of Energy awarded 577 contracts with an average award size of $10.8M. The Department of Energy's obligations are down 88.7% year over year compared with prior periods."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What categories and vendors dominate Energy's spending?",
        "body": "Facilities Support Services is the largest category at $3.5B, followed by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $1.1B. TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC is the largest vendor at $875M, followed by NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC at $633M and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $550M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Energy spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Energy obligated $6.2B in FY2027 to date. The Department of Energy awarded 577 contracts and the average award size was $10.8M. The Department of Energy's FY2027 total is partial and obligations are down 88.7% year over year compared with prior fiscal years."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Energy buy?",
      "a": "Facilities Support Services is the largest category, with $3.5B in obligations. The Department of Energy also spent $1.1B on Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences and smaller amounts across remediation, hazardous waste treatment, chemical manufacturing, and computer systems design."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Energy's largest contractors?",
      "a": "TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC is the largest contractor at $875M, followed by NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC at $633M, and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $550M. Other top vendors include CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC at $489M and SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC at $379M."
